      "problem": "${t}^{-1/6}=$",
      "worked_solution": "Remember that in general, a negative exponent can be converted to a positive exponent if we take the reciprocal. Here, we have:\n\n$$\n{t}^{-1/6}=\\frac{1}{{t}^{1/6}}\n$$\n\nNow, we can proceed as usual to convert the fractional exponent to a radical:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{{t}^{1/6}}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[6]{t}}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n$$\n{t}^{-1/6}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[6]{t}}\n$$",
